uation, therapy and outcome</article-title><source>Am J Med</source><year>1989</year><volume>86</volume><fpage>262</fpage><lpage>266</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">2919607</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/0002-9343(89)90293-3</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B24"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Crimlisk</surname><given-names>HL</given-names></name><name><surname>Bhatia</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Cope</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><name><surname>David</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Marsden</surname><given-names>CD</given-names></name><name><surname>Ron</surname><given-names>MA</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Slater revisited: 6 year follow-up study of patients with medically unexplained motor symptoms</article-title><source>BMJ</source><year>1998</year><volume>316</volume><fpage>582</fpage><lpage>586</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9518908</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B25"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Pennebaker</surname><given-names>JW</given-names></name></person-group><source>The psychology of physical symptoms</source><year>1983</year><publisher-name>New York: Springer-Verlag</publisher-name></citation></ref><ref id="B26"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Barsky</surname><given-names>AJMD</given-names></name><name><surname>Borus</surname><given-names>JFMD</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Functional Somatic Syndromes</article-title><source>Ann Intern Med</source><year>1999</year><volume>130</volume><fpage>910</fpage><lpage>921</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10375340</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B27"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Katon</surname><given-names>W</given-names></name><name><surname>Sullivan<